docker-cli: docker-cli (Docker command line client)
docker-cli:
docker-cli: docker is the command line client for the Docker Engine. It talks
docker-cli: to the daemon through its REST API and the Docker Unix socket to
docker-cli: build, run and manage containers, images, networks and volumes.
docker-cli:
docker-cli: This package is built from the official docker/cli sources and
docker-cli: also ships the docker-buildx plugin (BuildKit CLI) and shell
docker-cli: completions for bash, fish and zsh. Slackware 15.0, no systemd.
docker-cli:
docker-cli:
docker-cli: Home: https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/commandline/cli/